Redface 2 v0.42.8 — dev.

- New setting "keep private conversations cached on the device", under Private messages. Off by default.
- It is the only feature that writes your private messages to disk, hence the confirmation before enabling it.
- Turning it off erases immediately, and the bytes are actually overwritten — not merely the rows deleted.
- Signing out and switching accounts also erase the outgoing account's data.
